  "description": "PF7 backward from page 2 to page 1, which is the only case that reaches the MOVE at :369. The anchor is ZUSER001, row 1 of page 2, and the count is 2 so :248 pages backward. The READPREV at :343 discards the anchor, then the fill loop reads ten records downward - USER0005 into row 10 through to ADMIN001 into row 1 - and stops with WS-IDX at 0. The look-behind at :363 finds nothing below ADMIN001, so READPREV reports ENDFILE at :668-674: end of file is set and 'You have reached the top of the page...' is painted. Note 'top' here against case02's 'bottom' - the two arms are otherwise identical and swapping the literals would pass every other assertion. :364 then holds, because :245 SET NEXT-PAGE-YES unconditionally, and :365's first conjunct now fails, so the ELSE at :369 moves 1 into the count: the start of the file has been reached, so this is page 1 by definition however the count had drifted. :376 writes that 1 and :377 sends the map, so the final image shows page 00000001 under the end-of-file message.",
